  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">M.ASSIST: Moldovan Active Society, Stabilisation of Internal Social Tensions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Overall Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt; - Internal and external threats to peace and stability in Moldova during the period of national reforms and EU accession process anticipated and mitigated.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;Specific Objective&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt; &#xbf; Civil society actors can effectively collaborate with public authorities to improve equal access to quality public services, including for the most marginalized/vulnerable population; promote inclusive consultations on EU accession processes; and ensure social cohesion.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;O.1 Vulnerable people and marginalized groups have improved access to public services through CSO and public service providers, which contributes to prevent social unrest &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;O.2 CSO and public institutions increase their capacities to manage conflictive situations and reach agreements for community-local authorities-national government joint initiatives &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;O.3 Citizens, activists, grassroot organizations and local communities increase their awareness of ongoing reform processes and engage in social cohesion activities and conflict prevention mechanisms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
